# Backend Rules

## Layers
- **Domain**: entities, enums, value rules. No references to EF Core, ASP.NET or other projects.
- **Application**: use cases/services and interfaces (e.g. repositories) per module in `Modules/<Feature>/`.
  Maps between Domain entities and `Mostawsef.Contracts` DTOs.
- **Infrastructure**: `AppDbContext`, `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` classes in `Persistence/Configurations/`,
  repository implementations, external services. Registered through `AddInfrastructure(connectionString)`.
- **Api**: thin controllers (`api/[controller]`) that call Application services; no data access in controllers.
- **Contracts** (`shared/`): request/response DTOs only (records), no logic, no references.

## Database
- Configure entities with Fluent API configuration classes (auto-applied by `ApplyConfigurationsFromAssembly`), not attributes.
- Migrations live in Infrastructure; startup project is Api:
  `dotnet ef migrations add <Name> --project backend/Mostawsef.Infrastructure --startup-project backend/Mostawsef.Api`
- Connection string key: `ConnectionStrings:Default` (dev value in `appsettings.Development.json`, Docker PostgreSQL).
- Portability (SQLite fallback): no PostgreSQL-only types/functions or raw SQL; money as integer minor units.

## Auth (see `Docs/auth.md`)
- JWT bearer auth is on. Every new controller/endpoint needs `[Authorize]` or a role policy
  (`AuthPolicies.AdminOnly`, `AuthPolicies.SuperOnly`); only `login` and `health` are anonymous.
- Passwords go through `IPasswordHasher` (PBKDF2). Never store, log or return a password or hash.
- Role names come from `Mostawsef.Contracts.Auth.Roles` / `Domain.Enums.UserRole`.
- Secrets (`Jwt:Key`) are never committed for production; dev values live in `appsettings.Development.json` only.

## Conventions
- Async all the way with `CancellationToken` on I/O methods.
- Validate input at the API boundary; return proper status codes (400/404/409), never leak exceptions.
- Keep `GET /api/health` working: the desktop app relies on it.
